      <p style="font-size:0.94rem;color:var(--ink-soft);margin-top:0;">TLC enumerated the declared graph. The three deliberately reachable failure states violate the predicates below; no deadlocks were found. This is a phase-only teaching abstraction. It does not model real tensors, numerical precision, rewards, synchronization protocols, or trained-model behavior. The toggles select scenarios; their labels do not prove real-world guarantees.</p>
      <ul style="font-size:0.92rem;line-height:1.55;padding-left:20px;">
        <li><strong>NoFutureTokenLeakage:</strong> The model reaches the missing-mask failure in 3 transitions. Causal masking prevents future target leakage in the illustrated next-token training setup.</li>
        <li><strong>FiniteWeightsAndLoss:</strong> The injected non-finite failure is reachable in 6 transitions. Clipping finite gradients is useful, but does not repair NaN/Inf values or guarantee numerical stability.</li>
        <li><strong>NoRewardExploit:</strong> The reward-exploitation failure is reachable in 9 transitions. KL regularization discourages drift; it does not guarantee grounding, calibration or alignment.</li>
